-The three: a keeper notification, spoken delivery, and a push. A yes about one doesn't prove the others, but I'd rather have your rough sense of all three than a precise answer about one.
-
-WHY NOW: the message-delivery work just landed (#17086). Until tonight a message could be claimed by an agent that then died, and the row and the transcript would disagree about whether you got it — five confirmed losses. That's fixed and verified: `claimed` is now a real state in the database, a message whose claimer dies is released back to pending after a holdoff, and I watched one row go sent -> claimed -> claimer killed -> released at 48s -> re-fetched -> delivered, with the transcript confirming the model actually saw it.
-
-So the machinery is now honest all the way to the edge of your device. What nobody has ever checked is the last hop — whether the thing that leaves our side arrives on yours. Asking before this landed would have measured the old path, which is why it waited.
-
