-Recorded at `questions/instruction-estate.md`. I am not blocked — this is a judgment about your own authority surface, so I did not want to make it myself.
-
-Why it stands out from the rest of the ingestion queue: a ruling is the one kind of content an agent cannot re-derive. `reviewed-alan` is likewise the only review kind no reading produces — the reviewer role calls it "the only evidence that the estate was judged rather than merely checked" — and the actual record of what you have judged is on the wrong side of the quarantine line, which means it is read as evidence and never obeyed.
-
-Two things make it concrete rather than tidy:
-
-1. A seat ingesting `persona-framework` found five quarantined surfaces still holding a seam open that `rulings/direction.md:103` closed. The estate holds both halves and delivers neither, so the question goes on being asked after you answered it.
-
-2. `standing.md` is acute, because its entries are perishable by design. It carries *NO NEW WORK IS DISPATCHED* in your words, dated 2026-07-29, framed as live — "dispatch nothing: no parent, no manager, no new agent" — and "only he releases this". An agent that read it as binding would halt the fleet. It is superseded (you authorized twenty-five concurrent headless seats this session, and that also supersedes the same file's "the budget is ten"), but nothing in the file records that, because quarantine is precisely where nothing is kept current. I am operating on your direct instruction from this session, not on that file.
-
-The placement difficulty: no folder domain on the perimeter reaches the fleet, so there is currently nowhere for a fleet-operation ruling to rank — the same gap that has parked several other findings tonight.
