+++ b/personas/questions/pages/a-departure-on-the-domain-axis-has-no-spelling-should-the-na.question.context.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+seat-identity's third objective says a departure costs a compound naming only the axis that moved,
+`{persona}-{difference}`. Only the ROLE axis can actually be spelled: `an` composes
+`{persona}-{role}` and nothing else, and `ops agent classify`'s own help states "the domain is her
+row's — no name spells one".
+
+So `an ryn code-quality` composes the bare name `ryn`, reattaches her DEFAULT seat row, and pins
+`domain=code-quality`. The departure gets no name, is not separately addressable, and silently
+shares the default seat's row — while `ops agent send ryn` reaches one row either way.
+
+I raised this earlier and you ruled on the neighbouring question (bare persona addressing is the
+desired state, always-persona-role is obsolete) without touching this one. It is the last piece of
+objective 3 that is not being built: #17561 is in build against the bare-slug half and does not
+cover this.
+
+Either the objective's second half is wrong, or the code owes a spelling. I do not think either
+answer is obviously right and it turns on what you want a seat to BE, not on any fact I can measure.
