@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+ROOT CAUSE (last night's reboot was futile by construction): uinput IS compiled in Talos's kernel but EXCLUDED from the base image — Talos ships only a 245-module allowlist with zero input-subsystem modules. machine.kernel.modules LOADS, never INSTALLS. So #15805's config was correct but could never work, and no reboot could ever have fixed it. FIX: add the official siderolabs/uinput extension to our schematic + same-version upgrade (v1.12.9, no version bump, no reprovision, nvidia untouched). TARGET IS NODE-06, NOT node-03 — node-03 was only ever where the config happened to be declared. nimue proposed node-06, I ratified on capacity (32c/65.7GB/1.5TB free at 21%; node-04 has only 16GB RAM; node-02 is the DB primary; control-plane excluded on etcd latency). WHY THE REBOOT IS SAFE THIS TIME, unlike last night: (1) node-06 is FULLY DRAINABLE — postgrest/worker-supervisor/buildkit/realtime all hold NO local PVs so everything reschedules; node-03's git-transport+registry held hostPath PVs and COULDN'T move, which is exactly why that outage wedged CI fleet-wide. (2) talosctl upgrade --reboot-mode powercycle BYPASSES KEXEC, the exact path that hung node-03 and cost you a physical trip to the box. Worst case is now an empty drained node down until a power-cycle: no CI wedge, no service loss. Scope is keyboard/mouse only (uinput alone), derived from your bright line — gamepad emulation exists to drive gameplay, the forbidden category. Rig ships with hard cgroup limits day one: node-06 runs worker-supervisor, so an unlimited rig could OOM the supervisor running the agents that drive it. Full plan on #15805. Nothing else is blocked on this and nothing degrades if you'd rather wait.
