+Rebuilding persona `role` as foundational/shared/application/activity, reviewing in four batches.
+
+Definitions I'm using: foundational = systems the agents run on (if it breaks everything stops); shared = a system other domains build on but not the harness itself; application = a built product with its own users and deploy; activity = an area of your life a persona attends to, where the attending IS the work.
+
+Batch 1, activity (18 of 42): aria/ttrpgs, ceri/anime, eppie/performance-arts, grace/self-care, ione/sleep-hygiene, iris/litrpg-games, mari/arousal, nova/litrpg-books, zadi/literature, zeli/visual-arts, selah/prayer, talia/scripture-study, aelwyn/fitness, elaine/medicine, erin/chess, lali/mathematics, natalie/food, ruby/romance.
+
+Evidence the axis is real: all 10 current `companion` personas land here with nothing left over.
+
+Least sure: medicine and mathematics could read as `shared` knowledge rather than your activity. I put them in activity because the persona attends to YOUR health and YOUR learning, not a body of knowledge others consume.
+
+Also flagged, not this batch's question: self-care/sleep-hygiene/fitness are three health-adjacent domains with three personas, and literature/litrpg-books are two reading ones. Under 1-1, merging domains means retiring personas.
