+#16492 is verified and closed except this one item, which is yours because it is the last hop no agent
+can observe.
+
+Everything machine-checkable was checked: the notification is produced, it is keeper-scoped, it restarts
+nothing, and the latch stamps BEFORE the push — so a throwing push cannot re-arm it every tick. Without
+that latch it would have fired at you every 15 seconds for the whole window the keeper was down.
+
+What is left is delivery and wording, and only your device shows either.
+
+It fires when a keeper cannot be revived — a condition that used to be inferred from a low TLS-edge
+count (a proxy) and is now detected by watching a revival actually fail (the outcome). So when one of
+these reaches you, something is genuinely down rather than merely looking unusual.
+
+If it reads fine, #16492 closes and the tree is done.
